win32u, winemac.drv: Let the player stretch fixed-size windows.

Many games draw into a window of one fixed size, with a title bar but no
resizing border (Unity games by default). On a Mac that window can't be made
bigger, and on a Retina screen a 1440x800 game takes half the screen.

With StretchWindows (HKCU\Software\Wine\X11 Driver, next to EmulateModeset,
which it needs) such a window becomes resizable on the Mac. When the player
drags it, the window keeps its size for the program and win32u shrinks the
emulated display mode instead, so that the window covers the new raw rect:
the same virt -> raw mapping that EmulateModeset uses for full-screen games
then stretches GDI, OpenGL, Vulkan and DXMT output and maps the mouse back.
The program gets no WM_SIZE and no WM_DISPLAYCHANGE. The size the player chose
is kept per window class under HKCU\Software\Wine\EscApp\Stretch; when the
program sizes or shows the window itself, the scale is fitted to that size
again, keeping the program's aspect ratio, never below one program pixel per
screen pixel and never beyond the work area. A display mode the program set
itself is left alone.

winemac.drv keeps the aspect ratio while the player drags, sends no size-move
messages for such a window, and snaps the Cocoa frame to the exact size when
the drag ends, or at once after zoom or window tiling.

Bugs this exposed, fixed here because stretching makes them common:
- not every emulated mode works: the monitor DPI is a ratio of 16-bit numbers,
  so the virtual size is the nearest one that reduces far enough;
- win32u's framebuffer surface shares its client surface with the window
  drawable, which could take the update flag first, so the blit kept the old
  monitor size; it now reads the size at every present;
- winemac.drv sized the GL backing of a raw surface (the framebuffer under
  EmulateModeset) by its virtual rect, showing only a corner of the picture;
- viewWillDraw updated pending GL contexts through OnMainThread on the main
  thread itself and waited forever (Direct3D 9 games hung);
- the black bars around an emulated full screen ignored Retina mode;
- the client surface made for DXMT wasn't in win32u's list of used surfaces,
  so its view never followed the window.

